w: 2.~Me from their sec- ret coun- sel hide who do live wick- ed- ly;
w: 3.~Who do their tongues with ma- lice whet, and make them cut like swords;
w: 4.~That they may at the per- fect man in sec- ret aim their shot;
w: 5.~In ill en- cou- rage they them- selves, and their snares close do lay:
w: 6.~They have searched out i- ni- qui- ties, a per- fect search they keep:
w: 7.~God shall an ar- row shoot at them, and wound them sud- den- ly:
w: 8.~And on all men a fear shall fall, God’s works they shall de- clare;
w: 9.~In God the right- eous shall re- joice, and trust up- on his might;
